# Symphony Dossier Release & Build Standards

## Deployment Workflow
- The dossier deploys to GitHub Pages via `.github/workflows/symphony-pages.yml` when changes touch `symphony/**`.
- The live custom domain is `symphony.randybryanmoore.us`.

## Verification Steps
Before pushing changes that affect `symphony/`:
1. Check JavaScript syntax: `node --check symphony/script.js`
2. Test push script syntax: `python3 -m py_compile symphony/push_script.py`
3. Validate JSON manifests: `python3 -m json.tool symphony/release-manifest.json >/dev/null`
4. Rebuild the offline archive if files changed: `python3 symphony/push_script.py --build`
5. Verify digests and release integrity: `python3 symphony/push_script.py --verify`

## Post-Deploy Stamping
After GitHub Actions deploys `main`:
- Run `python3 scripts/stamp_release.py` to capture and stamp the exact GitHub Actions workflow run ID and conclusion into the release manifests.
